    {
      "title": "Seven reported bomb threats against European flights confirmed as false alarms – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/nov/03/zelenskyy-berlin-merz-europe-sweden-spain-france-belgium-poland-latest-news",
      "description": "<p>Bomb threats were made on routes involving a number of airlines, including Ryanair and WizzAir</p><p><strong>Back to Poland, Warsaw Modlin airport <a href=\"https://www.modlinairport.pl/aktualnosc/wznowienie-operacji-lotniczych-na-lotnisku-warszawamodlin-komunikat-nr-30311-1150\">says</a> it has resumed operations after an earlier bomb threat</strong> – but a part of the airport where the London flight was parked remain closed and is being checked by security forces.</p><p><strong>Ukraine’s</strong> <strong>Zelenskyy has said his talks with Merz and Germany’s president Steinmeier </strong>will focus on “diplomatic coordination” on air defence and energy sector.</p><p><em>“These will be the priorities of today’s talks. We all have an interest in security, stability, and protecting the rules-based international order. And we must work together to turn these principles into concrete decisions and actions.”</em></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/nov/03/zelenskyy-berlin-merz-europe-sweden-spain-france-belgium-poland-latest-news\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-03T18:22:57"
    },
    {
      "title": "Seven planes across Europe searched or diverted after ‘malicious hoax’ bomb threats",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/03/four-planes-flying-across-europe-targeted-by-bomb-threats",
      "description": "<p>Unclear if series of incidents affecting two UK departures and a number of Ryanair services among others are connected</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/nov/03/zelenskyy-berlin-merz-europe-sweden-spain-france-belgium-poland-latest-news\">Europe live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>At least seven planes around Europe were searched or diverted after a series of bomb threats to passenger flights on Tuesday.</p><p>Two UK departures and a number of Ryanair flights were threatened in what the UK government called “malicious hoaxes”, after all planes landed safely and no explosives were found.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/03/four-planes-flying-across-europe-targeted-by-bomb-threats\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-03T17:32:45"
    },
